# devices/akita/drivers/camera/conf: the Pixel 8a's camera side (docs/drivers-config.md, docs/porting/drivers.md).

driver AKITA_TORCH
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.akita_torch.c
	help    the Pixel 8a's flashlight: the LM3644 flash driver on zuma's hsi2c@10980000 (USI14 of PERIC0, brought up here),
	help    a look (torch=1), lit once (torch=2), Darwin's through /dev/hakios-torch (torch=3); never above torch_max_ma
	help    (100), off after torch_max_s (30), on a fault or a warm skin

driver AKITA_CAMERA
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.akita_camera.c
	requires AKITA_ACPM
	help    the Pixel 8a's three cameras from the start: their buses (PERIC0's USI1-3), clocks (CMU_TOP's CIS_CLKn), pins and
	help    power (the S2MPG15's camera I/O rail and GPIOs, the SLG51002 camera PMIC) as the device tree has them; a look
	help    (camera=1), nothing written
